This license governs the use of VECTRA: Versatile Experience and Career
Template for Research and Academia ("VECTRA", "the Template", or "the
Project").

VECTRA is a source-available LaTeX CV and resume template made available for
personal academic, professional, and application use under the terms below.

This license is not an open-source license as defined by the Open Source
Initiative. It grants limited rights to use the Template while restricting
redistribution, republication, commercial exploitation, and derivative template
distribution.

1. Definitions

1.1. "Template Source" means all source files, style files, class files,
documentation, examples, build scripts, configuration files, and other materials
included in the VECTRA repository, including but not limited to files in:

    src/
    docs/
    examples/
    cv/main.tex
    Makefile
    latexmkrc
    README.md
    NOTICE
    USAGE_POLICY.md

1.2. "User-Editable Content Files" means files explicitly intended for users to
edit for the purpose of creating their own CV or resume content, including:

    cv/profile.tex
    cv/settings.tex
    cv/sections/*.tex

and equivalent profile, settings, or section files in example directories when
used only as a starting point for personal CV or resume content.

1.3. "Generated Documents" means PDF files or other output documents generated
by compiling VECTRA with user-provided personal content.

1.4. "Official Repository" means the official VECTRA repository maintained by
Yixuan Huang:

    https://github.com/yixnhuang/vectra

If the repository URL changes, the official repository is the location
designated by Yixuan Huang as the authoritative source for VECTRA.

1.5. "Commercial Use" means use primarily intended for commercial advantage,
monetary compensation, paid services, resale, redistribution as part of a
commercial product, inclusion in a paid template collection, or use in providing
CV, resume, design, consulting, recruiting, or document-preparation services to
others for compensation.

Personal use of Generated Documents for academic applications, fellowship
applications, job applications, internship applications, personal websites, or
professional self-presentation is not considered Commercial Use under this
license.

2. Grant of Permission

Subject to the terms of this license, you are granted a limited, non-exclusive,
non-transferable, non-sublicensable license to:

2.1. Download or clone the Template Source from the Official Repository for
personal use.

2.2. Edit User-Editable Content Files for the purpose of creating your own CV,
resume, academic profile, application document, or similar personal document.

2.3. Compile the Template with your own content to create Generated Documents.

2.4. Use, submit, upload, print, email, publish, or otherwise share your
Generated Documents for personal academic, professional, and application
purposes.

2.5. Share or recommend VECTRA by linking to or citing the Official Repository.

3. Generated Documents

3.1. You retain ownership of your own personal content, including your name,
contact information, education history, work history, research experience,
projects, awards, publications, skills, and other user-provided information.

3.2. Generated Documents created by filling VECTRA with your own personal
content may be used and shared without visible attribution to VECTRA or Yixuan
Huang.

3.3. This license does not require your generated CV or resume PDF to display a
license notice, citation, watermark, footer attribution, or visible credit.

3.4. If you publicly describe, recommend, review, or share the Template itself,
you must cite or link to the Official Repository.

