Repository.

4.2. Publish a modified version of the Template Source.

4.3. Create, distribute, or publish another template, repository, package,
project, product, or service based on VECTRA or any substantial portion of the
Template Source.

4.4. Incorporate VECTRA into another public or private template collection,
template gallery, resume builder, document generator, software package, or
repository intended for redistribution.

4.5. Sell, license, sublicense, rent, lease, or commercially exploit VECTRA or
any modified version of VECTRA.

4.6. Use VECTRA to provide paid CV, resume, application, design, document
preparation, recruiting, or consulting services to third parties without prior
written permission from Yixuan Huang.

4.7. Remove, obscure, or alter copyright notices, license notices, repository
references, or attribution notices contained in the Template Source.

4.8. Misrepresent VECTRA as your own template or imply that your modified
template source is an official version.

4.9. Use the name "VECTRA", "Yixuan Huang", or related project branding to imply
endorsement, sponsorship, or affiliation without prior written permission.

5. Permitted Content Editing

5.1. You may modify User-Editable Content Files to create your own CV or resume.

5.2. You may add, remove, or reorder CV entries inside User-Editable Content
Files.

5.3. You may replace example personal information with your own information.

5.4. You may not modify Template Source files for the purpose of creating,
publishing, redistributing, or maintaining a modified template.

6. Sharing and Citation

6.1. To share VECTRA with others, link to or cite the Official Repository.

6.2. You may not upload, mirror, or repost copies of the Template Source.

6.3. Suggested citation format:

    Yixuan Huang. VECTRA: Versatile Experience and Career Template for Research
    and Academia. GitHub repository:
    https://github.com/yixnhuang/vectra

